# Normalize line endings in the repository, not in each contributor's editor.
#
# Without this, a checkout on Windows or an editor configured for CRLF rewrites
# whole files and every diff becomes unreadable. `text=auto` lets git detect
# text files, and `eol=lf` forces LF in the working tree so scripts, prompts,
# and datasets are byte-identical on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated and binary artifacts must never be line-ending normalized, or the
# bytes change and the files stop being valid images/PDFs.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary

# Datasets are read as CSVs and prompts are hashed into run manifests, so both
# must be LF-only for fingerprints to be reproducible across platforms.
*.csv text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
